Measurement-only source edit for the hand-on census (never committed as code):
the census binary of the handoff prediction is built from the tree with this
one change, so the refused hand-on rule withdraws nothing and every leak the
cast-return tree still reports is recorded with its witness. The cast-return
rule stays on. The edit is reverted before any other build.

--- a/crates/qcore-c-gateway/src/legacy_refused_operands.rs
+++ b/crates/qcore-c-gateway/src/legacy_refused_operands.rs
@@ pub(super) fn apply(
     read: &BTreeSet<usize>,
     diagnostics: &BTreeSet<LegacyDiagnostic>,
 ) {
+    let _ = (&output, read, diagnostics);
+    return;
     if !read.is_empty() && refused(diagnostics) {
         withdraw(output, read);
     }
 }
